 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<p>Based on the recipe in <i>Easy Korean Cooking</i>, made with your methods (coarse salt, ceramic grater, cheesecloth for the juices).</p>",
   "title_html": "Source"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Autumn and winter radish is sweet and mild.</li><li>Radish from other seasons can taste bitter — add a little extra sugar to balance it.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Which radish"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Fish sauce can stand in for either, though the Korean sauces taste better and are worth seeking out.</p>",
   "title_html": "Salted anchovy and shrimp sauce"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Plain kombu stock — see the <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">kombu dashi</a> page, or soak a piece of kombu in water.</p>",
   "title_html": "Kelp stock"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Kimchi keeps best in a cold fridge, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 °C</span>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Storage"
  }
 ],
