   "title": "Make the filling",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Tip the drained cubes into the paste with the green onions and toss until each cube is red all over.</li><li>Gloves help — the chili stains.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Mix the drained cubes with the filling and green onions — gloves on.",
      "src": "illustrations/kkakdugi/4-how1.webp?v=0db3f1cb6a"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kkakdugi/4.webp?v=08e88eb267",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pack it into a container with a tight lid and let it ferment in the fridge for <b>5–7 days</b> before you eat it.</li><li>Around <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 °C</span></b> is the ideal fridge temperature for kimchi.</li></ul>",
